    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a2">

                <pb facs="0706" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg620"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. De Long to
                        their Excellencies Oyeno Kagenori, acting minister for
                        foreign affairs of His Imperial Japanese Majesty, and Aurelio Ga y Garcia,
                        envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of Peru in Japan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation, Yokohama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            15, 1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The undersigned, acknowledging the receipt
                    of your communication addressed to him of date the 14th instant, with respect to
                    the disposition of the bark Maria Luz, begs leave in reply to state that as a
                    matter of accommodation he will forthwith comply with the request you make. The
                    undersigned begs leave to assure your excellency of his high and most
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. DE LONG.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
